# Little Browser (Android): a window per profile (docs/ux.md §5; docs/android-ui.md,
# Multi-profile). A browser window's profile is the one its intent names
# (app.littlebrowser.lb.profiles.Profiles), the default one unless it says, and its profile
# provider gives that profile, loading it first if need be, instead of "the last used regular
# profile"; a window destroyed while its profile loads gets none. Other activities (settings,
# history, downloads, ...) keep the last used profile, and what else Chromium asks of it follows
# the window in front, which records itself as such (Profiles.setLastUsed). A new window that
# Chromium opens from a browser window (New window, Open in new window, moving tabs to a new
# window) is of that window's profile. The shell opens another profile's window through
# Chromium's multi-window launch, reopening the profile's own Chromium window (and its tabs) if
# it had one, into that window while it is open; Recents lists only the window last in front.

diff --git a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/init/ActivityProfileProvider.java b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/init/ActivityProfileProvider.java
